---
export const prerender = true;

import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// "Last updated" is the deploy date.
const today = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — rootfast"
  description="What rootfast does and doesn't collect."
>
  <article class="max-w-content mx-auto px-6 lg:px-10">
    <p class="pt-6 text-xs text-ink-3">
      <a href="/" class="link-hover">Index</a>
      <span class="mx-2">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-2">Privacy</span>
    </p>

    <header class="pt-10 pb-8">
      <p class="label flex items-baseline gap-3">
        <span aria-hidden="true">⚘</span>
        <span>Policy &middot; last updated {today}</span>
      </p>
      <h1 class="mt-5 font-serif text-4xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl leading-none text-ink">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 font-serif text-xl italic text-ink-2">
        the short version: rootfast collects almost nothing.
      </p>
    </header>

    <hr class="rule-strong" />

    <section class="py-10 grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-8 space-y-10 text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink">What we don't do</h2>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm">
            <li>● No user accounts. There is nothing to sign up for.</li>
            <li>● No tracking cookies, pixels, fingerprinting, or cross-site identifiers.</li>
            <li>● No advertising, affiliate links, or remarketing.</li>
            <li>● No selling, sharing, or trading any data about you.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink">What is collected</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
            The site runs on Cloudflare. Cloudflare keeps standard edge-server logs
            (IP address, timestamp, request URL, user-agent, response status) for
            operational purposes — abuse mitigation, debugging, and DDoS protection.
            Cloudflare's own privacy notice governs how those logs are handled and
            for how long.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
            Rootfast itself does not write any user-identifying data to its
            database. The API ingests USDA + GBIF + iNaturalist data and returns
            it; it does not record who asked.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink">Cloudflare Analytics</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
            Rootfast uses
            <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="link-hover text-ink">Cloudflare Analytics</a>
            to understand aggregate traffic — total page views, referrers,
            country-level geography, and broad browser / device categories.
            This data is collected <em>without cookies</em>, without any
            persistent identifier across visits, and without cross-site
            tracking. Individual visits are not profiled and cannot be linked
            to you on return. Cloudflare processes the data on our behalf and
            does not sell it.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
            If you'd rather not be counted at all, any standard ad- or
            tracking-blocker that blocks Cloudflare's insights endpoints will
            exclude you with no effect on the rest of the site.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink">Third-party content</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
            Some pages embed images served directly from iNaturalist's open-data
            CDN (<span class="mono">inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com</span>).
            Loading those images causes your browser to connect to AWS
            infrastructure. We attach no identifiers; the request is whatever
            your browser sends by default.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
            Links out to plants.usda.gov, gbif.org, itis.gov, and similar are
            standard hyperlinks — clicking them takes you to those sites under
            their own policies.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink">Contact form</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
            If you reach out via the <a href="/contact" class="link-hover text-ink">contact form</a>,
            your name, email, and message are forwarded by a Cloudflare Worker
            (operated by Gold Dust Web) through SendGrid to a mailbox we monitor.
            The submitting IP is briefly retained for rate-limiting (one hour)
            and then discarded. Messages themselves live in the recipient
            mailbox until manually deleted; they are used only to reply to your
            inquiry.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink">Children</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
            Rootfast does not knowingly collect any data about anyone, and
            therefore does not knowingly collect data about children. The
            content is general botanical reference material suitable for all ages.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink">Changes</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
            If this policy materially changes, the updated text replaces this
            page and the date at the top of the page changes. There is no
            mailing list to notify.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="lg:col-span-4 lg:pl-10 lg:border-l lg:border-rule">
        <p class="label">In one line</p>
        <p class="mt-3 font-serif text-lg italic text-ink-2 leading-snug">
          Rootfast doesn't want your data. It wants you to read plant records.
        </p>

        <hr class="rule mt-8" />

        <p class="label mt-8">Questions</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
          Use the <a href="/contact" class="link-hover text-ink">contact form</a>
          for anything privacy-related.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
